<main class="doc" id="main">
  <div class="doc__in">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">VisiSocial is a research project. It asks one question: if someone analysed your social-media data, what could they conclude, and on what evidence?</p>
    <h2>Approach</h2>
    <p>Earlier tools showed people what could be inferred about them. VisiSocial separates what you did from what was computed and from what a model guessed, and links each finding to the items it came from so you can check it yourself.</p>
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>A prototype. It runs only for the Facebook test accounts allowed by the app's settings. Its methods are published with their measured weaknesses, and it has not yet been evaluated with real participants.</p>
    <h2>Author</h2>
    <p>Farhan Khan, independent researcher. The first version of VisiSocial began as a final-year project at Swansea University; this version was rebuilt independently.</p>
    <p>Code, prompts, test fixtures and evaluation results are released under the MIT licence at <a href="https://github.com/farhankhan5825/visisocial">github.com/farhankhan5825/visisocial</a>.</p>
  </div>
</main>
